      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The pricing structure for moving and packing services can vary depending on several factors, including the distance covered, the volume of goods, and the special handling requirements for fragile items. Additionally, GST (Goods and Services Tax) and documentation costs contribute to the overall cost.</p>
<p>In this analysis, we will explore the pricing aspects for a 850 km route in West Bengal and focus on keywords like "movers and packers rate in West Bengal" and "movers and packers in Sanpada charges."</p>

<table style="width:100%">
  <tr>
    <th>Pricing Element</th>
    <th>Description</th>
    <th>Example Cost</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Base Distance Charge</td>
    <td>A fixed cost for covering the initial distance (850 km) for the move.</td>
    <td>For example, a base distance charge of $250 for the 850 km journey.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Volume-based Freight Rates</td>
    <td>A cost calculation based on the volume of the shipment.</td>
    <td>For instance, a volume-based freight rate of $0.5 per cubic meter for a 10-meter cube shipment.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Special Handling Fees for Fragile Items</td>
    <td>Additional charges for handling delicate or valuable items.</td>
    <td>A special handling fee of $10 per fragile item negotiated at a rate of $5 per hour for careful handling.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>GST (Goods and Services Tax)</td>
    <td>A 18% tax on the total moving cost.</td>
    <td>For the given example, a GST cost of 18% on (250 + (0.5 * 10) + 10 * 1) = $28.5</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Documentation Costs</td>
    <td>Fees for preparing and delivering necessary paperwork.</td>
    <td>For instance, a documentation cost of $50 for meticulous processing and delivery.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>In West Bengal, movers and packers typically charge a base price for covering the initial distance of 850 km between the starting and destination points. This base distance charge is generally $250.</p>

<p>Next, the cost is based on the volume of the shipment. Assuming a rate of $0.5 per cubic meter, a 10-meter cube shipment would incur an additional charge of $25 ($0.5 * 50).</p>

<p>For fragile items, special handling fees may be applied. For instance, a fee of $10 per fragile item and a rate of $5 per hour for careful handling results in an additional cost of $100 ($10 * 20).</p>

<p>GST (Goods and Services Tax) is a 18% tax on the total moving cost. In this scenario, the GST cost would be $28.5 (18% of ($250 + $25 + $100)).</p></div>
